field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407122 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407091 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407122 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "ff69c2a4-0b39-5df0-a3c8-8543d321044e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407097 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407100 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407104 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407110 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184000" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=6p+10q+3,$ where $p,q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2dfcbd6d-7083-5b50-9b60-a0306b88077d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407123 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNow, note the following regarding the expression $6p+10q+3:$\n\n- All terms, apart from the constant term, have a common factor of $2.$\n\n- The constant term can be written as $3=2+1.$\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{odd}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =6p+10q+3 \\\\  & =(6p+10q+2)+1 \\\\  & =2({{3p+5q+1}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=3p+5q+1\\in Z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407099 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407102 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407112 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407117 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184062" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=4i+2j-8,$ where $i,j\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f34688d-9a70-5e5f-86f3-8ad4e9bec34c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407124 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNotice that all terms in the expression $4i+2j-8$ have a common factor of $2.$ \n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{even}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =4i+2j-8 \\\\  & =2({{2i+j-4}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=2i+j-4\\in Z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407098 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407105 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407118 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184102" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=10m+4,$ where $m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45d8a589-5d18-5ea9-a082-e4a7691a3a49" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407125 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is even since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =10m+4 \\\\  & =2({{5m+2}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=5m+2,$ which is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407101 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407115 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407119 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407121 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184080" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-1,$ where $m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56052108-5098-50da-941c-873f362e867d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407126 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNow, note the following regarding the expression $6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-1:$\n\n- All terms, apart from the constant term, have a common factor of $2.$\n\n- The constant term can be written as $-1=-2+1.$\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{odd}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-1 \\\\  & =(6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-2)+1 \\\\  & =2({{3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-1}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-1$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407111 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407116 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407120 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407122 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184073" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=2{q}^{8}+14{q}^{4}-4,$ where $q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "796608cf-7d3e-5b3b-bbf0-417e641244c1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407127 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNotice that all terms in the expression $2{q}^{8}+14{q}^{4}-4$ have a common factor of $2.$ \n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{even}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =2{q}^{8}+14{q}^{4}-4 \\\\  & =2({{{q}^{8}+7{q}^{4}-2}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a={q}^{8}+7{q}^{4}-2$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407103 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407107 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407109 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184131" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=-10b-5,$ where $b\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is odd." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7aad35dc-2cee-5fa5-8937-92b9fde54d6b" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407128 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-10q-5 \\\\  & =(-10b-6)+1 \\\\  & =2({{-5b-3}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-5b-3,$ which is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407106 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407108 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407113 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184128" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=1-8p,$ where $p\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is odd." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89ca628f-f5b6-5773-9b1c-0f25806d7d8c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407129 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =1-8p \\\\  & =(-8p)+1 \\\\  & =2({{-4p}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-4p,$ which is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407095 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407096 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407114 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184120" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $n=-10-30q,$ where $q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "988b9965-fc57-5a1f-a7d2-bc319da35474" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407130 #edb/ref 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is even since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-10-30q \\\\  & =2({{-5-15q}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-5-15q,$ which is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
